# Pin line endings so `manifest.sha256` stays reproducible off-tree.
#
# W01-D1: this repository ships a byte-level integrity manifest. With
# core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, a fresh clone checked every text file
# out as CRLF while the manifest had been computed over LF worktree bytes — 233 of
# 234 entries failed verification on a clean clone (independent QA reproduction).
# Pinning eol=lf makes the checkout bytes identical to the bytes the manifest hashes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be normalised.
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.db binary

# Test fixtures: a PDF is hashed as bytes by tools/w03/verify-reading-loop.mjs, so a
# checkout that normalises it would change the recorded source hash.
*.pdf binary
